BIB                 12         34                                 M0151  1    2 
TITLE      Charge distribution of residual nuclei at              M0151  1    3 
            photospallation of Nb-93.                             M0151  1    4 
AUTHOR     (H.A.Vartapetyan,E.O.Grigoryan,A.S.Danagulyan,         M0151  1    5 
            N.A.Demekhina,A.G.Khudaverdyan)                       M0151  1    6 
INSTITUTE  (4ARMJER)                                              M0151  1    7 
REFERENCE  (J,YF,34,289,1981)                                     M0151  1    8 
           (J,SNP,34,163,1981) - Eng.trans.of YF,34,289,1981      M0151  1    9 
FACILITY   (SYNCH,4ARMJER)                                        M0151  1   10 
INC-SOURCE (BRST)                                                 M0151  1   11 
METHOD     (ACTIV)                                                M0151  1   12 
DETECTOR   (GELI)                                                 M0151  1   13 
ERR-ANALYS The systematic errors amounted to 10-15%.              M0151  1   14 
COMMENT    The charge distribution of residual nuclei at          M0151  1   15 
            spallation of Nb-93 by bremsstrahlung photons with    M0151  1   16 
            maximum gamma energy of 4.5 GeV was investigated.     M0151  1   17 
           Studying the isobar charge dispersion and comparing    M0151  1   18 
            the obtained data with results of hardronic nuclear   M0151  1   19 
            reactions one is able to elucidate some regularities  M0151  1   20 
            of the nuclear spallation as well as to predict the   M0151  1   21 
            production probability of yields of the residual      M0151  1   22 
            nuclei which are difficult to measure by activation   M0151  1   23 
            methods. To estimate the reaction yield quantitatevelyM0151  1   24 
            a five-parameter rudstam formula was used.            M0151  1   25 
           The nature and properties of isobaric and mass yields  M0151  1   26 
            are discussed and compared with calculations of the   M0151  1   27 
            two-step cascade-evaporation model.                   M0151  1   28 
STATUS     (TABLE) Data are published in form of tables.          M0151  1   29 
